Goal: each job can keep its conversation as an append-only file, one JSON object per line.

Do: create internal/agentjob/loopmsg.go with:
type LoopMessage struct { Seq int `json:"seq"`; Role string `json:"role"`; Content json.RawMessage `json:"content"`; Tokens int `json:"tokens,omitempty"`; At time.Time `json:"at"` }
func (s *Store) MessagesPath(id string) string  // filepath.Join(s.JobDir(id), "messages.jsonl")
func (s *Store) AppendMessages(id string, msgs ...LoopMessage) ([]LoopMessage, error)
func (s *Store) Messages(id string) ([]LoopMessage, error)

AppendMessages: read the current last Seq (0 if the file is missing), give each new message the next Seq (1, 2, 3 ...) and At = time.Now().UTC() when zero, open the file with os.O_APPEND|os.O_CREATE|os.O_WRONLY mode 0o644, write all lines in ONE Write call (so they land together), call f.Sync(), close, and return the messages with their Seq set. Messages: read the file line by line; a missing file returns nil, nil; a last line that is not valid JSON (a write cut off by a crash) is ignored, any other bad line is an error. Use bufio.Reader, not bufio.Scanner (lines can be longer than 64 KB).

Tests (internal/agentjob/loopmsg_test.go): TestAppendMessagesAssignsSeq (two calls, Seq continues 1,2,3); TestMessagesMissingFile; TestMessagesIgnoresTornLastLine (append half a JSON line by hand, Messages returns the good ones); TestMessagesLongLine (a 200 KB content).

